2f39\",\n    \"text\": \"A complex is an integrated subset with Φ greater than zero that is not contained in a larger subset with higher Φ, and complexes are the loci of subjective experience.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-a-distributed-thalamocortical-network-is-well-suited-to-generate-consciousness-b--571db463385d\",\n    \"source_id\": \"source-01-an-information-integration-theory-of-consciousness-w2114900706--09db8f102f39\",\n    \"text\": \"A distributed thalamocortical network is well suited to generate consciousness because it combines functional specialization with functional integration.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-an-8-week-mindfulness-based-stress-reduction-course-improves-endogenous-orientin--f7bde69b7431\",\n    \"source_id\": \"source-02-mindfulness-training-modifies-subsystems-of-attention-w2132002500--696402dc8f78\",\n    \"text\": \"An 8-week mindfulness-based stress reduction course improves endogenous orienting relative to control and retreat groups at post-training testing.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-anatomical-or-functional-disconnection-within-thalamocortical-systems-can-reduce--89adceb072c5\",\n    \"source_id\": \"source-01-an-information-integration-theory-of-consciousness-w2114900706--09db8f102f39\",\n    \"text\": \"Anatomical or functional disconnection within thalamocortical systems can reduce, split, or selectively alter consciousness by changing the system’s integrated-information structure.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-consciousness-corresponds-to-a-system-s-capacity-to-integrate-information-becaus--ca44bbf79dcb\",\n    \"source_id\": \"source-01-an-information-integration-theory-of-consciousness-w2114900706--09db8f102f39\",\n    \"text\": \"Consciousness corresponds to a system’s capacity to integrate information, because conscious experience is both highly differentiated and unified.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-consciousness-is-graded-rather-than-all-or-none-and-could-in-principle-exist-in--76ebdb9cb6bc\",\n    \"source_id\": \"source-01-an-information-integration-theory-of-consciousness-w2114900706--09db8f102f39\",\n    \"text\": \"Consciousness is graded rather than all-or-none and could in principle exist in infants, animals, or artificial systems when they possess complexes with sufficiently high Φ.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-each-particular-conscious-experience-is-specified-by-the-current-activity-values--ef679659733b\",\n    \"source_id\": \"source-01-an-information-integration-theory-of-consciousness-w2114900706--09db8f102f39\",\n    \"text\": \"Each particular conscious experience is specified by the current activity values of the variables that mediate informational interactions within a complex.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-mindfulness-training-can-improve-attention-related-behavior-by-changing-specific--f9e8e6ee54d7\",\n    \"source_id\": \"source-02-mindfulness-training-modifies-subsystems-of-attention-w2132002500--696402dc8f78\",\n    \"text\": \"Mindfulness training can improve attention-related behavior by changing specific attentional subsystems rather than producing a single global attention benefit.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-participants-with-prior-concentrative-meditation-experience-show-reduced-conflic--7b44607a9505\",\n    \"source_id\": \"source-02-mindfulness-training-modifies-subsystems-of-attention-w2132002500--696402dc8f78\",\n    \"text\": \"Participants with prior concentrative meditation experience show reduced conflict-monitoring interference at baseline relative to meditation-naive participants.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-post-training-conflict-monitoring-differences-are-not-detected-among-the-mbsr-re--62de62c3ee08\",\n    \"source_id\": \"source-02-mindfulness-training-modifies-subsystems-of-attention-w2132002500--696402dc8f78\",\n    \"text\": \"Post-training conflict-monitoring differences are not detected among the MBSR, retreat, and control groups, possibly because task repetition improves conflict scores in controls.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-reticular-sensory-afferent-motor-efferent-and-subcortical-loop-activity-can-modu--173db43834c9\",\n    \"source_id\": \"source-01-an-information-integration-theory-of-consciousness-w2114900706--09db8f102f39\",\n    \"text\": \"Reticular, sensory afferent, motor efferent, and subcortical loop activity can modulate or affect the thalamocortical main complex without directly contributing to conscious experience.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-strongly-modular-neural-architectures-can-be-computationally-sophisticated-yet-c--212c143093c3\",\n    \"source_id\": \"source-01-an-information-integration-theory-of-consciousness-w2114900706--09db8f102f39\",\n    \"text\": \"Strongly modular neural architectures can be computationally sophisticated yet contribute little to consciousness because they generate many small low-Φ complexes rather than one high-Φ complex.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-attention-network-test-separates-alerting-orienting-and-conflict-monitoring--08b2302acb19\",\n    \"source_id\": \"source-02-mindfulness-training-modifies-subsystems-of-attention-w2132002500--696402dc8f78\",\n    \"text\": \"The Attention Network Test separates alerting, orienting, and conflict monitoring by subtracting performance across predefined cue and target conditions.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-attentional-effects-should-be-treated-as-preliminary-because-the-study-used--8a181621f4d7\",\n    \"source_id\": \"source-02-mindfulness-training-modifies-subsystems-of-attention-w2132002500--696402dc8f78\",\n    \"text\": \"The attentional effects should be treated as preliminary because the study used small groups, no active-training control, behavioral measures only, and imperfect control over training protocols.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-quality-of-consciousness-is-specified-by-the-informational-relationships-amo--52a77799b51d\",\n    \"source_id\": \"source-01-an-information-integration-theory-of-consciousness-w2114900706--09db8f102f39\",\n    \"text\": \"The quality of consciousness is specified by the informational relationships among the elements of a complex, represented as an effective-information-defined qualia space.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-quantity-of-consciousness-available-to-a-system-is-measured-by-the-value-of--48abc06d417d\",\n    \"source_id\": \"source-01-an-information-integration-theory-of-consciousness-w2114900706--09db8f102f39\",\n    \"text\": \"The quantity of consciousness available to a system is measured by the Φ value of a complex, where Φ is effective information across the minimum information bipartition.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim_id\": \"claim-within-the-retreat-group-greater-prior-meditation-experience-predicts-a-smaller--3ca73021a60e\",\n    \"source_id\": \"source-02-mindfulness-training-modifies-subsystems-of-attention-w2132002500--696402dc8f78\",\n    \"text\": \"Within the retreat group, greater prior meditation experience predicts a smaller Time 2 alerting score, consistent with a more readied attentional state.\"\n  }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
