{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p /Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/mind/runs/run-20260426T110455Z--i0ytd7tpj8/semantic && cat > /Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/mind/runs/run-20260426T110455Z--i0ytd7tpj8/semantic/topic_generation.json <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"topics\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Differentiated and Integrated Mental Functions\\\",\n      \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n      \\\"sections\\\": [\n        \\\"Frame the topic as a cautious bridge between two levels of analysis: Tononi treats consciousness as differentiated-yet-unified information integration, while Jha, Krompinger, and Baime treat attention as separable alerting, orienting, and conflict-monitoring subsystems rather than one global attention capacity.\\\",\n        \\\"Summarize the information-integration basis: consciousness is proposed to depend on complexes that integrate information, and thalamocortical organization is emphasized because it combines functional specialization with functional integration.\\\",\n        \\\"Summarize the attentional-subsystem basis: the Attention Network Test separates alerting, orienting, and conflict monitoring, and mindfulness training history is associated with different changes across these subsystems.\\\",\n        \\\"Develop the synthesis around subsystem organization: both sources support analyzing mind in terms of specialized components and their coordination, while resisting a single undifferentiated measure of mental function.\\\",\n        \\\"State the evidential boundary clearly: the mindfulness study reports preliminary behavioral attention effects and does not show that mindfulness training changes integrated information, Φ, complexes, or consciousness itself.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"claim-consciousness-corresponds-to-a-system-s-capacity-to-integrate-information-becaus--c